# =========================
# Node
# =========================
node_modules/
# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. Committing it pins the whole
# transitive dependency tree, so builds are reproducible and a compromised patch
# release of any dependency can't reach production unreviewed. It also makes it
# possible to answer "were we running the bad version?" after a disclosure.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

